o":[]},{"nodeId":"HosRc0hczubBHrWxCzEJj","fullDescription":"","title":"How to Calculate Complexity?","resources":[],"prerequisites":[{"nodeId":"VotdHk0_bI3CeoIf-KoKu","title":"Algorithmic Complexity"}],"description":"","order":99,"leadsTo":[]},{"nodeId":"v0LrabYYOKzV4oCXOK2Rs","fullDescription":"","title":"Asymptotic Notation","resources":[],"prerequisites":[{"nodeId":"VotdHk0_bI3CeoIf-KoKu","title":"Algorithmic Complexity"}],"description":"","order":100,"leadsTo":[]},{"nodeId":"WzFkdkcbL8ea9DBkjfSwa","fullDescription":"","title":"Sorting Algorithms","resources":[],"prerequisites":[{"nodeId":"VotdHk0_bI3CeoIf-KoKu","title":"Algorithmic Complexity"}],"description":"","order":101,"leadsTo":[]},{"nodeId":"OkdM_PJge70j5tsjT2Esl","fullDescription":"# Go\n\nGo is a statically typed, compiled language designed for simplicity and performance. It is increasingly popular in backend and infrastructure roles and is commonly used at companies like Uber, Cloudflare, and Docker. Its syntax is minimal, and its concurrency model is distinctive, but for LeetCode purposes, what matters is its straightforward standard library and fast execution. Go does not have a built-in generic data structure library as rich as Java or C++, so you will sometimes need to implement things like heaps from scratch using the container/heap interface. It is a good choice if Go is your day-to-day language.","title":"Go","resources":{"type":"roadmap","title":"Visit the Dedicated Go Roadmap","url":"https://roadmap.sh/golang","_id":"6a60910cfcaecc259f0e7a80"},"prerequisites":[{"nodeId":"Z4uVzAoNzcAkyjd-lp3_M","title":"Pick a Language"}],"description":"# Go\n\nGo is a statically typed, compiled language designed for simplicity and performance. It is increasingly popular in backend and infrastructure roles and is commonly used at companies like Uber, Cloudflare, and Docker. Its syntax is minimal, and its concurrency model is distinctive, but for Leet...","order":102,"leadsTo":[]},{"nodeId":"gjZZOwmYkXQHPfg9Ynz80","fullDescription":"# Java\n\nJava is one of the most commonly used interview languages, especially at large companies with backend and enterprise codebases. Its type system is verbose but explicit, and the standard library is comprehensive with well-documented data structures including priority queues, linked lists, and tree maps. Java forces you to think about types and interfaces clearly, which can actually help structure your thinking on harder problems. The main downside for interview prep is boilerplate: simple operations require more lines than in Python or Ruby. If Java is your primary language, it is a strong and widely accepted choice.","title":"Java","resources":{"type":"roadmap","title":"Visit the Dedicated Java Roadmap","url":"https://roadmap.sh/java","_id":"6a60910cfcaecc259f0e7b6e"},"prerequisites":[{"nodeId":"Z4uVzAoNzcAkyjd-lp3_M","title":"Pick a Language"}],"description":"# Java\n\nJava is one of the most commonly used interview languages, especially at large companies with backend and enterprise codebases. Its type system is verbose but explicit, and the standard library is comprehensive with well-documented data structures including priority queues, linked lists, and...","order":103,"leadsTo":[]},{"nodeId":"HVD9G3JlLBsAg111vQILj","fullDescription":"# JavaScript\n\nJavaScript is a solid choice if you already use it professionally or are preparing for frontend-focused roles. Its array methods and object literals are expressive, and most algorithmic patterns translate naturally to it. The main limitation is that JavaScript lacks a built-in heap or priority queue, so you will need to implement one or use a library when heap problems arise. If you are comfortable with JavaScript and do not want to switch languages just for interviews, it is a perfectly valid choice.","title":"JavaScript","resources":{"type":"roadmap","title":"Visit the Dedicated JavaScript Roadmap","url":"https://roadmap.sh/javascript","_id":"6a60910cfcaecc259f0e7a81"},"prerequisites":[{"nodeId":"Z4uVzAoNzcAkyjd-lp3_M","title":"Pick a Language"}],"description":"# JavaScript\n\nJavaScript is a solid choice if you already use it professionally or are preparing for frontend-focused roles. Its array methods and object literals are expressive, and most algorithmic patterns translate naturally to it. The main limitation is that JavaScript lacks a built-in heap or ...","order":104,"leadsTo":[]},{"nodeId":"Z4uVzAoNzcAkyjd-lp3_M","fullDescription":"","title":"Pick a Language","resources":[],"prerequisites":[],"description":"","order":105,"leadsTo":[{"nodeId":"HVD9G3JlLBsAg111vQILj","title":"JavaScript"},{"nodeId":"gjZZOwmYkXQHPfg9Ynz80","title":"Java"},{"nodeId":"OkdM_PJge70j5tsjT2Esl","title":"Go"},{"nodeId":"9h1mz0xAUvPrnRm9VndJF","title":"Ruby"}]},{"nodeId":"9h1mz0xAUvPrnRm9VndJF","fullDescription":"# Rust\n\nRust is a systems programming language focused on memory safety and performance without a garbage collector. It is gaining popularity for roles in systems programming, WebAssembly, and performance-critical applications. For LeetCode, Rust is the most challenging language to use due to its strict ownership model, which can make pointer-heavy problems like linked lists and trees significantly more complex to implement than in other languages. If you are already comfortable with Rust and want to use it for interviews, it is possible and impressive, but it is not recommended as a starting point for interview preparation.","title":"Ruby","resources":{"type":"official","title":"Visit the Dedicated Rust Roadmap","url":"https://roadmap.sh/rust","_id":"6a60910cfcaecc259f0e7c48"},"prerequisites":[{"nodeId":"Z4uVzAoNzcAkyjd-lp3_M","title":"Pick a Language"}],"description":"# Rust\n\nRust is a systems programming language focused on memory safety and performance without a garbage collector. It is gaining popularity for roles in systems programming, WebAssembly, and performance-critical applications. For LeetCode, Rust is the most challenging language to us